Subject: [PATCH] R80b, part 6, patch 9 (cld-advisor, at main's word in M16;
 main's third folder, section 2, row A1): B1892'S PAGE AND VERDICT LINE GIVE
 THE COUNT THAT ITS OWN TABLE GIVES

A reader's check of main's answers at Review 80 (agy-002's; row A1, held by main: both sentences are on the
page). The table of B1892's section 5 was corrected to sum to 53 for the first reader and 43 for the second.
A note main added to the same page in the same commit says that the first reader has 52 findings.

Counted here, by a function now in the arc's lock: 16 rows; 53 and 43; 9 found by both; 87 in all.

The note's own conclusion rests on the 52: "each reading found half or more of what the two found
together". With 52 the second reading found 43 of 86, which is half. With 53 it found 43 of 87, which is
just under half. The verdict line says the same in its fourth correction.

What is changed, with the old words kept:
  - the page: a dated bracket after the one that says 52. It gives the table's sums, 87 in all, and says
    that the first reading found more than half and the second just under half;
  - the verdict line: a fifth correction after the fourth, in the same words. It names no session;
  - the lock: the table is counted, and the page and the verdict line are held to the count. With one
    number of one row changed the count changes.

THIS REWORDS A CONCLUSION OF MAIN'S BY ONE FINDING, and it is main's to reword again: "half or more" holds
for the first reading only. Nothing else of the page is touched. The two generated pages that carry the
verdict line are made again.

The arc's lock passes: 6 tests. Every gate passes but the count of landings.
The row is held by main; the count is this lock's own.

BUILT AGAIN ON MAIN'S 663a902ff (2026-11-13): main corrected B1892's page itself at Review 81 (the web seat's finding 4):
its bracket gives 53, as the table sums, and says the conclusion holds. This patch now leaves the page and the verdict
line as main wrote them, and brings only the lock: the table of section 5 counted (16 rows; 53, 43, 9 found by both; 87
together), the count held to fail when one number changes, and main's bracket held after the one that said 52. SENT BACK
TO MAIN: by the table, the second reading found 43 of the 87 that the two found together, which is under half, so "each
reading found half or more" holds for the first reading and not for the second; main's bracket says the conclusion holds.
